<article class="story-column">
<p class="story-column__kicker">01 &middot; Our Story</p>
<h2>A Standard Set Before Service</h2>
<p>MKG exists for the cooks, chefs, restaurants, hospitality teams, and serious home kitchens that understand the details are not separate from the experience. They are the experience taking shape.</p>
</article>
<article class="story-column">
<p class="story-column__kicker">02 &middot; Our Standard</p>
<h2>Care, Restraint, and the Right Edge</h2>
<p>Every knife is inspected before it is sharpened: steel, profile, bevel, damage, wear, and intended use all matter. The goal is not simply to make a knife sharp. The goal is to restore confidence, preserve the life of the blade, and help the tool feel right again.</p>
</article>
<article class="story-column">
<p class="story-column__kicker">03 &middot; Our Method</p>
<h2>Inspect. Correct. Sharpen. Finish.</h2>
<p>Poorly maintained tools slow the work, dull the mood, and make &ldquo;good enough&rdquo; easier to accept. When the tools are right, the standard rises. Prep becomes cleaner. Movement becomes smoother. The kitchen works with more confidence.</p>
</article>
</section>

<!-- Closing -->
<section class="story-closing" aria-label="MKG philosophy">
<p>Do kitchens that care keep their tools sharp?<span>Or do sharp tools help keep the kitchen caring?</span></p>
<small>Maybe it does not matter.</small>
<strong>Either way, the standard is set before the plate reaches the table.</strong>
</section>

